  "worked_solution": "First, we must find the elements of the set $B.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {3,4,5,6,7}$ into the formula $5n,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=3 & \\,\u21d2\\,5(3)=15 \\\\ n=4 & \\,\u21d2\\,5(4)=20 \\\\ n=5 & \\,\u21d2\\,5(5)=25 \\\\ n=6 & \\,\u21d2\\,5(6)=30 \\\\ n=7 & \\,\u21d2\\,5(7)=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nB={15,20,25,30,35}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $B\u2286A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A\u2286B$ is false, while $A\u2288B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $A\u2287B$ is equivalent to $B\u2286A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\".",
